# The coverage matrix. Everything under matrix/ is GENERATED, and the line
# between what is versioned and what is not is NOT "generated or written by
# hand" -- it is "can this be reproduced from what the repository contains".
#
# It cannot. The inputs are an RTX 2070, a pinned driver, a guest and a night
# of runs; `catalog` needs traces, and traces need the card. So the reports
# and the evidence files are the RECORD OF A MEASUREMENT, closer to a lab
# notebook than to a build artefact, and a clone without the hardware would
# otherwise carry a matrix/ that can never be filled. They are also the half
# a reader wants: small, plain text, and each one carries the driver, the
# card, the kernel and the commit it was measured on.
#
# Versioned (nothing to do -- no rule below matches them):
#   DISCOVERY.md PROBES.md MATRIX-<drv>.md TASKS-<drv>.md
#   catalog-<drv>.md   the report a person reads
#   catalog-<drv>.json the same rows plus what only a machine wants -- the
#                      rm_status histograms above all, which are the
#                      fingerprint a guest run is compared against
#   guest-<drv>.json    what a run inside a VM found, per probe
#   verified-<drv>.json which answers matched a native run, and over how
#                       many bytes
#
# Not versioned: the raw measurement they are derived from. Tens of megabytes
# of tsv and strace output that `trace` and `guest` regenerate in minutes ON
# A RIG, and that no diff is ever read.
#
# A new artefact goes in if it is a claim somebody could act on, and stays
# out if it is the raw material of one.
/matrix/traces/
/matrix/.tables.txt
